  "worked_solution": "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{2}$ term and the constant term. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing terms with zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\n-9{x}^{3}+22x\\,=\\,-9{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+22x+0\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+4x-2 \\\\  & -3x+4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,-9{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+22x+0\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-9{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-12{x}^{2}+22x+0 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,12{x}^{2}+16x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+0 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,6x-8}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $3{x}^{2}+4x-2,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $8.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-9{x}^{3}+22x}{\\,-3x+4\\,} & =3{x}^{2}+4x-2+\\frac{8}{-3x+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
